Located four kilometers from Melbourne's CBD, the semi-industrial area had a checkered past. Even though it was gaining popularity with students and young people looking to take advantage of the cheap rent, it still had a reputation as one of Victoria's roughest suburbs. Crime rates were high and drugs and gangs were an ongoing problem. But for 27-year-old Susan Bartlett, who went by Sue, Collingwood offered everything she needed. There was a milk bar on the corner, reliable public transport nearby, and it wasn't far from the high school where she worked as an art teacher. The house at 147 Easy Street was basic but cozy, and the rent was much more affordable than the place in nearby Richmond where she had been living previously. Furthermore, Sue was looking forward to living with her friend, 28-year-old Suzanne Armstrong.
该地区距离墨尔本中央商务区四公里，是一个半工业区，有着复杂的过去。尽管它因廉价的租金而受到学生和年轻人的欢迎，但它仍被认为是维多利亚州最混乱的郊区之一。犯罪率很高，毒品和帮派问题一直存在。但对于27岁的苏珊·巴特利特（大家都叫她苏）来说，科林伍德提供了她所需要的一切。街角有一家奶吧，附近有可靠的公共交通，而且离她担任美术老师的高中也不远。Easy街147号的房子虽然简陋但很舒适，租金也比她之前住的附近的里士满便宜得多。此外，苏很期待与她的朋友、28岁的苏珊·阿姆斯特朗住在一起。

8
00:07:12.000 --> 00:08:12.000
The two knew one another from high school, having both grown up in the country town of Benalla. The women had a lot in common. Both were intelligent, creative and sociable, and they shared a love of cooking and travel. They'd recently explored the Greek islands together, proving they could live alongside one another without issue. Sue also had a great affection for Suzanne's toddler son, Gregory. By January 1977, Sue and Suzanne had been living in Collingwood together for around two months. Monday, January 10 started normally for both women. They rose early, ate breakfast together, and then went their separate ways. Suzanne bathed Gregory, and the two took off on her bicycle to visit some friends. Sue's mother was in town, and the two met to go shopping in the city.
两人从高中就认识了，都是在贝纳拉小镇长大的。她们有很多共同点。两人都很聪明、有创造力且善于交际，并且都热爱烹饪和旅行。她们最近一起探索了希腊群岛，证明了她们可以毫无问题地住在一起。苏也非常疼爱苏珊的幼儿格雷戈里。到1977年1月，苏和苏珊已经在科林伍德一起住了大约两个月。1月10日星期一，对两人来说开始得很正常。她们早起，一起吃早餐，然后各奔东西。苏珊给格雷戈里洗了澡，两人骑自行车去拜访了一些朋友。苏的母亲当时在城里，两人见面去城里购物。

9
00:08:12.000 --> 00:09:17.000
Afterwards, Sue went home to work on a dress she was in the process of sewing. She was a talented seamstress who made most of her own clothes, and she intended to wear this dress on a date she had planned for Wednesday night. After working on the dress for a while, Sue began to cook dinner in preparation for company. Sue's brother Martin was a regular visitor to 147 Easy Street. Having also made the move to the big city from Benalla, he enjoyed helping his sister with tasks around the house in exchange for a home-cooked meal. Sue's stereo had recently broken, so Martin agreed to come over for dinner and then have a go at fixing it. Martin got the stereo working, and they all listened to some records, but then Sue and Suzanne said they wanted to watch television. One of their favorite shows, The Sullivan's, was about to start, and they were keen to see it once Suzanne put her son down for the night.
之后，苏回家继续缝制一件连衣裙。她是一位才华横溢的裁缝，大部分衣服都是自己做的，她打算在周三晚上的约会中穿这件裙子。在缝纫了一会儿后，苏开始做晚饭，准备招待客人。苏的哥哥马丁是Easy街147号的常客。他也从贝纳拉搬到了大城市，喜欢帮妹妹做家务，以换取一顿家常便饭。苏的音响最近坏了，所以马丁答应过来吃晚饭，顺便修一下。马丁修好了音响，他们一起听了一些唱片，但后来苏和苏珊说她们想看电视。她们最喜欢的节目之一《沙利文一家》即将开始，她们很想在苏珊哄儿子睡觉后观看。

10
00:09:17.000 --> 00:10:33.000
At around 9pm, Martin bid the women farewell, with the Bartlett siblings making plans to catch up again the following week. It was an enjoyable, albeit uneventful evening. Everyone was in good spirits, and nothing seemed out of the ordinary. When Martin left, Suzanne and Sue were comfortably settled in front of the television. He would become the last person to see his sister and her friend alive. Given there were no further sightings of either of the women after Martin left, and that dog was found wandering the streets the following day, it was determined they had likely been killed sometime in the early hours of Tuesday, January 11. Neighbors didn't hear or see anything out of the ordinary, although next-door neighbor Alona recalled hearing Gregory crying for a prolonged period on Tuesday morning. This meant that the bodies of Susan Bartlett and Suzanne Armstrong lay undiscovered in their home for three days, while the young boy lay distressed and alone in his cot.
晚上9点左右，马丁向她们告别，巴特利特兄妹计划下周再聚。这是一个愉快但平淡的夜晚。每个人都心情愉快，一切看起来都很正常。马丁离开时，苏珊和苏正舒适地坐在电视机前。他成了最后一个见到他妹妹及其朋友活着的人。由于马丁离开后没有人再见过这两名女性，且第二天狗被发现独自在街上游荡，据推测她们很可能是在1月11日星期二凌晨被杀害的。邻居们没有听到或看到任何异常，尽管隔壁邻居阿洛娜回忆说，周二早上听到格雷戈里长时间地哭泣。这意味着苏珊·巴特利特和苏珊·阿姆斯特朗的尸体在她们家中被放置了三天未被发现，而那个小男孩则独自在婴儿床里感到痛苦。

11
00:10:33.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Collectively, the young women had been stabbed a total of 82 times, with Sue sustaining 55 stab wounds to Suzanne's 27. The wounds were deep, having likely been inflicted using forceful rapid thrusts with a 2.5cm wide blade. Suzanne had also been raped post-mortem. However, it didn't appear that any great struggle had taken place. Other than a vase of flowers that had been knocked over, Suzanne's bedroom was in relatively neat order. The blood had pulled on the carpet above her head, several drops of blood stained her bedsheet, and a pair of her underwear lay beside her. The scene indicated that Suzanne had been reading in bed when she got up and encountered her killer, who then launched a brutal and frenzied attack. There were also smears of blood on the lamp and alarm clock next to the bed.
总的来说，这两名年轻女性总共被刺了82刀，苏被刺了55刀，苏珊被刺了27刀。伤口很深，很可能是用2.5厘米宽的刀刃猛烈快速地刺入造成的。苏珊在死后还遭到了强奸。然而，现场似乎并没有发生激烈的搏斗。除了一个被打翻的花瓶外，苏珊的卧室相对整洁。地毯上在她头部上方有血迹，床单上有几滴血，她的一件内衣掉在旁边。现场表明，苏珊当时正在床上看书，起身时遇到了凶手，随后遭到了残酷而疯狂的袭击。床边的台灯和闹钟上也有血迹。

12
00:11:38.000 --> 00:12:47.000
Either Suzanne had reached over in an attempt to grab her bedside phone to call for help, or the killer had reached over to turn the lamp off. The location of Sue Bartlett's body in the hallway, just outside of Suzanne's bedroom, suggested she had likely confronted the killer after Suzanne was already dead. Sue's hands and arms were covered with the fence wounds, which explained the smears of blood on the hallway walls. Investigators believed that after killing Sue, the perpetrator returned to Suzanne's bedroom to rape her lifeless body. The attack had been so quick and savage that neither woman had any time or opportunity to seek help. Gregory was discovered in the middle room between the two women's bedrooms. He was found lying hungry in his cot, his skin pale and nappy soiled. Other than having been dehydrated and distressed for some time, he was alive and unhurt.
要么是苏珊伸手试图抓起床边的电话求救，要么是凶手伸手关掉了台灯。苏·巴特利特的尸体位于走廊里，就在苏珊卧室外，这表明她很可能是在苏珊遇害后与凶手对峙的。苏的手和手臂上布满了防御性伤口，这解释了走廊墙壁上的血迹。调查人员认为，在杀害苏之后，凶手回到了苏珊的卧室，强奸了她冰冷的尸体。袭击发生得如此迅速和残忍，以至于两名女性都没有时间或机会寻求帮助。格雷戈里是在两名女性卧室之间的中间房间被发现的。他被发现时正饿着肚子躺在婴儿床里，皮肤苍白，尿布脏了。除了脱水和痛苦了一段时间外，他活着且没有受伤。

13
00:12:47.000 --> 00:13:44.000
His room, which doubled as Sue's sewing room was relatively tidy and didn't appear to have been touched during the attack. Sue's bedroom at the end of the hall was similarly neat and there was no blood. Smudges of blood were discovered in the bathroom, specifically in the bathtub. Blood pooled around the plug hole and small bone splinters were found in the crook of the drain. This suggested that the killer had showered after carrying out the murders, with the bone fragments having likely been washed from their knife. The knife itself was nowhere to be found. Small spots of blood were also found on the lid of the washing machine. The killer might have used the machine or at least considered doing so.
他的房间兼作苏的缝纫室，相对整洁，袭击过程中似乎没有被触动。走廊尽头的苏的卧室同样整洁，没有血迹。在浴室里，特别是在浴缸里发现了血迹。血汇集在排水孔周围，排水管的弯头处发现了细小的骨头碎片。这表明凶手在行凶后洗了澡，骨头碎片很可能是从他们的刀上洗下来的。刀本身不见踪影。洗衣机盖上也发现了小血点。凶手可能使用了洗衣机，或者至少考虑过这样做。

