00:13:44.000 --> 00:14:49.000
The living room revealed further evidence of the killer's attempt to clean themselves up. A small blood-soaked tower lay on the couch. A second blood-soaked tower was found at a playground 300 metres from number 147 on Wellington Street. As DNA testing wasn't available in the late 70s, it couldn't be determined whether any of the blood belonged to the killer. Sue's blood type was Type O and Sue'sans was Type A, both common blood groups. Only Type A blood was found in Sue'sans bedroom, the bathroom and on the blood-soaked towers, while only Type O blood was found smeared in the hallway. This either meant that the killer wasn't wounded during the attacks or that he shared a common blood type with one of his victims. However, he did leave one undisputable piece of evidence behind.
客厅揭示了凶手试图清理自己的进一步证据。沙发上放着一条浸满血迹的毛巾。在距离147号300米处的惠灵顿街游乐场发现了第二条浸满血迹的毛巾。由于70年代末没有DNA检测技术，无法确定这些血迹是否属于凶手。苏的血型是O型，苏珊的是A型，都是常见的血型。在苏珊的卧室、浴室和浸满血迹的毛巾上只发现了A型血，而走廊里只发现了O型血。这要么意味着凶手在袭击中没有受伤，要么意味着他与其中一名受害者血型相同。然而，他确实留下了一个无可辩驳的证据。

